Sofia, I then got out at the station in Potsdam.
I walked from there directly into the town.
The sun shone wonderfully.
Locals and visitors strolled together through the streets.
Everyone came outside in the spring sunshine.
People met everywhere on the streets.
I walked past many small shops.
Many families rode their bicycles.
The people talked and laughed.
No one hurried.
I just walked along with the large crowd.
We walked slowly across old squares.
A few musicians played on the street.
I stopped briefly and listened.
I liked that very much!
After that, I strolled further towards the park.
